WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.360
Every dye particle in this glass moves at random.

2
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.060
None of them has a direction.

3
00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.040
So why does a drop of colour always spread out, and almost never gather back into a

4
00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:16.040
drop?

5
00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.390
Let's zoom in and build a model.

6
00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:22.370
Picture a tank split down the middle by an open line.

7
00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.810
Most of the purple dots start on the left.

8
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:28.510
Only a few start on the right.

9
00:00:29.533 --> 00:00:31.813
Each dot jiggles along its own path.

10
00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:36.253
Any dot that reaches the line may hop across, either way.

11
00:00:37.473 --> 00:00:39.293
No dot knows where the crowd is.

12
00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:42.013
And nothing pushes any of them.

13
00:00:43.017 --> 00:00:46.877
So over many seconds, which way will more dots cross on average?

14
00:00:48.257 --> 00:00:50.477
From left to right, or from right to left?

15
00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:52.557
Pause and decide.

16
00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:01.733
On average, more cross from left to right.

17
00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:04.153
No dot chose that.

18
00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:07.653
There are simply more dots on the left to make the hop.

19
00:01:08.933 --> 00:01:10.133
A few still hop back.

20
00:01:11.353 --> 00:01:15.193
In a short count, luck can make a tie, or even tip it the other way.

21
00:01:16.233 --> 00:01:19.293
How crowded a substance is in a space has a name.

22
00:01:20.893 --> 00:01:24.213
Concentration is how much of a substance is in a given space.

23
00:01:25.333 --> 00:01:28.133
At the start, the left side is more concentrated.

24
00:01:29.417 --> 00:01:30.737
Keep the hops running.

25
00:01:31.937 --> 00:01:34.517
The crowd thins on the left and grows on the right.

26
00:01:35.677 --> 00:01:39.917
This drift, from more concentrated to less concentrated, is called diffusion.

27
00:01:41.117 --> 00:01:43.177
Now the two sides are about even.

28
00:01:44.657 --> 00:01:47.977
Dots still cross, and over time just as many go each way.

29
00:01:49.117 --> 00:01:52.397
The colour stops changing, yet the dots never stop moving.

30
00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:56.100
Now swap the open line for a cell membrane.

31
00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:00.240
On one side is the blood, crowded with oxygen.

32
00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:04.240
Inside a muscle cell, there is much less of it.

33
00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.340
The same random hops carry more oxygen into the cell than out of it.

34
00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:15.360
Carbon dioxide is more crowded inside the cell, so it drifts out, the other way.

35
00:02:16.433 --> 00:02:18.973
The cell spent no energy on any of this.

36
00:02:20.113 --> 00:02:25.413
Movement across a cell membrane that needs no energy from the cell is called passive

37
00:02:25.413 --> 00:02:26.413
transport.

38
00:02:27.133 --> 00:02:28.513
So here is the rule.

39
00:02:29.893 --> 00:02:34.493
Particles move at random, so on average more leave a crowded side than come back.

40
00:02:35.693 --> 00:02:38.393
That makes a one-way drift, with no push needed.

41
00:02:39.433 --> 00:02:43.633
But what if the crowded particle is one the membrane will not let through?

42
00:02:44.933 --> 00:02:47.373
And what if water is the only thing that can cross?

43
00:02:48.613 --> 00:02:49.793
That is the next film.
